
! Vertical tunnelling transport through monolayer graphene: from a point tip
! above the sheet into an infinite, featureless substrate plane below it.
!
! This answers a different question from an STM image. Task 9003 (and upstream
! task 162) plot what a tip SEES -- the vacuum local density of states at the
! tip position, the Tersoff-Hamann picture. Task 9005 computes what gets
! THROUGH: the electron enters at a point r above the material and leaves into
! a metal underneath, so the current is set by the NONLOCAL Green's function
! between the two,
!
!   T(r;E) = int_plane |G(r,r';E)|^2 d^2r'
!   G(r,r') = sum_kn psi_kn(r) psi*_kn(r') / (E - eps_kn + i eta)
!
! A substrate invariant under every lateral lattice translation conserves the
! lateral momentum, so the k-sum is incoherent and only bands at the SAME k
! interfere on the way out. What survives is one Hermitian matrix per k-point
! -- the bands' Gram matrix restricted to the exit plane,
! S_k[n,n'] = int_plane psi*_kn psi_kn' -- and the whole transmission is one
! quadratic form, T(r;E) = sum_k w_k sum_nm a_n(r) a*_m(r) S_k[n,m].
!
! Task 9005 writes S_k and the tip amplitudes psi_kn(r_p) to
! ELKPY_TRANSPORT.OUT. The energy weighting and the contraction are two dozen
! lines of Python (elkpy.parsers.transport) rather than Fortran, deliberately:
! they are then unit-testable against synthetic data, and an energy sweep
! costs nothing extra since neither the wavefunctions nor S_k depend on E.
!
! For MONOLAYER graphene the answer is a theorem. The states at the Fermi
! level are the Dirac doublet at K, and the symmetry the tip/substrate
! geometry leaves intact -- C3v, whose mirror exchanges the two sublattices
! without flipping z -- still acts irreducibly on that pair. By Schur's lemma
! S_K is a multiple of the identity: the substrate cannot tell the partners
! apart, there is nothing off-diagonal for the current to interfere through,
! and the transmission map IS the tunnelling image. Stack a second layer
! (AB-stacked, so the low-energy states become layer-polarized) and it is not.
!
! Note the transport k-grid below is generated and diagonalised by the task
! itself, so it is independent of ngridk and of reducek. It must be a multiple
! of 3 to contain K -- graphene's states at E_F all sit there, and on a mesh
! without it the map is identically zero, not merely small.
!
! This is an elkpy extension: it needs an elk binary built by build_elk.sh
! (which applies patches/), not stock Elk.
!
! Run:   elk                       (in this directory, ~2 minutes)
! Plot:  python3 plot_transport.py

tasks
  0
  9005

! MANDATORY. Elk otherwise relocates the origin -- onto the inversion centre,
! which for a honeycomb is the bond midpoint -- while the plot2d and exit
! planes below stay in the frame written here. The two would then sit on the
! wrong side of the sheet, which the task refuses rather than computes.
tshift
  .false.

! the exit (substrate) plane: normal to the third lattice vector, at
! fractional coordinate 0.38 -- 2.4 Bohr below the sheet, in the vacuum. The
! plane is spanned by the other two lattice vectors, which is what makes the
! exit integral an exact orthogonality relation rather than a quadrature.
elkpy_transport_exit
  3   0.38

! export every state within this window (Hartree, relative to the Fermi
! energy). The on-shell weight applied on the Python side kills the rest, so
! this is what keeps the file small
elkpy_transport_window
  -0.04   0.04

! the transport k-grid: generated here and diagonalised fresh, so it needs no
! relation at all to ngridk below. A multiple of 3 contains K
elkpy_transport_kgrid
  6  6  1

! the TIP plane, in the usual plot2d block: 2.4 Bohr above the sheet, the same
! standoff as the exit plane below it. The material must lie BETWEEN them
plot2d
  0.0  0.0  0.62
  1.0  0.0  0.62
  0.0  1.0  0.62
  24  24

avec
  4.647926   0.000000   0.000000
 -2.323963   4.025000   0.000000
  0.000000   0.000000  20.000000

atoms
  1                                        : nspecies
  'C.in'                                   : spfname
  2                                        : natoms
  0.00000000  0.00000000  0.50000000    0.0 0.0 0.0
  0.33333333  0.66666667  0.50000000    0.0 0.0 0.0

sppath
  '../../vendor/elk/species/'

ngridk
  6  6  1

rgkmax
  7.0

nempty
  10
